{"step_index":98,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-30T14:01:42Z","input_tokens":2556,"cache_read_tokens":121165,"output_tokens":1585,"content":"The Flask server is **running live right now in the background!**\n\nYou can test and explore the entire application right away.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Open the Application in Your Browser\nClick or navigate to this URL in your web browser:\n### **👉 [http://127.0.0.1:5000](http://127.0.0.1:5000)**\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Step-by-Step Test Guide (What to Try)\n\nFollow this 5-minute interactive test checklist to see all features working together:\n\n#### 1. Explore the Overview Dashboard (`Section 1`)\n- Notice the **KPI summary cards** at the top: *Registered Today*, *Waiting Patients*, *In Consultation*, *Avg Predicted Wait Time*, *Active Doctors*, and *Bed Occupancy*.\n- Observe the **Patients Waiting by Department** bar chart and the **Diurnal Patient Arrivals** line chart (showing actual vs predicted arrivals).\n- Check the **Department-Wise Status** cards with color-coded badges: **GREEN** (Normal), **ORANGE** (Warning), and **RED** (Critical).\n\n#### 2. Test Dynamic Waiting Time Prediction (`Section 4`)\n- Click **4. Wait Time Prediction** in the left sidebar.\n- In the search box, enter token number **`101`** (or `143`) and click **Predict Waiting Time**.\n- You will see the AI breakdown:\n  - **OPD Token #** & **Assigned Doctor** (with clinic room and availability)\n  - **Patients Ahead in Queue**\n  - **Predicted Waiting Time** (calculated by the Random Forest model)\n  - **Expected Consultation Time** (e.g. `10:45 AM`)\n  - **Explainability Factors** (triage priority code, doctor speed, etc.).\n\n#### 3. Test Dynamic Consultation Delay Cascading (`Section 3`)\n- Click **3. Patient Queue** in the sidebar.\n- Look at **Dr. Rajesh Sharma's clinic**:\n  - You will see a patient currently in consultation (e.g. Token #101).\n  - Note the predicted waiting time and expected consultation time of the waiting patients below them (e.g., Token #102: *10 mins*, `10:35 AM`).\n- Click the yellow **Record Delay** button on the active consultation and type **`20`** (for a 20-minute delay).\n- **Watch what happens:** The system immediately cascades the 20-\n<truncated 1108 bytes>\n\n- View the **+1h, +2h, +3h, +4h** forecast columns and the forecast trend chart.\n- Click **Simulate Admission (+1 Bed)** or **Simulate Discharge (-1 Bed)** at the top right to see the occupancy percentages and charts update in real time.\n\n#### 6. Test Disease Outbreak & Inventory Linkage (`Section 8 & 9`)\n- Click **8. Disease Trends** in the sidebar.\n- Review the 14-day history chart showing an escalating Dengue trend and tomorrow's projected cases.\n- Click the button **Simulate Dengue Spike (+15)** at the top right.\n- Now switch to **9. Inventory**:\n  - Notice that **Dengue NS1 Antigen Rapid Test Kits** and **IV Normal Saline** immediately trigger a **CRITICAL Shortage Alert** because of the disease surge.\n  - Click **Restock** next to the item, enter `150`, and watch the stock level recover to Normal (Green).\n\n#### 7. Test the Hackathon Simulation Lab (`Section 12`)\n- Click **12. Simulation Lab** in the sidebar.\n- Here you can test everything simultaneously:\n  - Inject a burst of **+10 Normal Patients** or **+3 Emergency Patients**.\n  - Toggle a doctor's status to **On Break**.\n  - If you ever want to restart from the beginning, click **Reset Simulation to Baseline**.\n\n#### 8. Inspect the Machine Learning Evaluation (`Section 13`)\n- Click **13. ML Performance** in the sidebar.\n- View the real validation metrics computed on the test split:\n  - **Random Forest:** $R^2 \\approx 0.996$, $\\text{MAE} \\approx 10.0\\text{ mins}$, $\\text{RMSE} \\approx 13.7\\text{ mins}$.\n  - **Linear Regression Baseline:** $R^2 \\approx 0.860$, $\\text{MAE} \\approx 59.7\\text{ mins}$.\n  - View the **Feature Importance** chart explaining which factors influence wait times the most (`patients_ahead`, `avg_consult_duration`, `priority_code`, etc.).\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: How to Run It in Any Terminal (For Later)\n\nIf you reboot your computer or want to launch it from a new terminal window:\n\n```powershell\ncd \"C:\\Users\\KRUTIKA SHIVANAND\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\queue-oracle\"\npython app.py\n```\nThen simply open `http://127.0.0.1:5000` in your browser.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
