{"step_index":114,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-30T15:00:34Z","input_tokens":3015,"cache_read_tokens":130537,"output_tokens":915,"content":"The project is **already saved on your laptop**! \n\nI have also packaged everything into a single, clean **ZIP archive** (`queue-oracle.zip`, 1.6 MB) so you can easily copy it to your Desktop, upload it to GitHub, or put it on a USB pendrive.\n\n---\n\n### Method 1: Open the Folder Right Now in Windows File Explorer (Easiest)\n\n1. On your keyboard, press **`Windows Key + R`** (this opens the Run dialog).\n2. Copy and paste this exact path into the box:\n   ```text\n   C:\\Users\\KRUTIKA SHIVANAND\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\n   ```\n3. Click **OK** (or press Enter).\n4. Windows File Explorer will open directly to your project files! You will see two items:\n   - 📁 **`queue-oracle`** — The complete uncompressed project folder with all source code, datasets, trained machine learning models, database, and web files.\n   - 📦 **`queue-oracle.zip`** — The ready-to-share 1.6 MB zip file.\n\nYou can now right-click either the folder or the zip file and **Copy** it to your **Desktop**, **Downloads**, **Documents**, or a USB drive.\n\n---\n\n### Method 2: Copy to Your Desktop Using PowerShell\n\nIf you prefer to copy it to your Desktop using a command, open **PowerShell** or **Command Prompt** on your laptop and run:\n\n```powershell\n# Copy the full project folder directly to your Desktop:\nCopy-Item -Path \"C:\\Users\\KRUTIKA SHIVANAND\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\queue-oracle\" -Destination \"$HOME\\Desktop\\queue-oracle\" -Recurse\n\n# And copy the ready-to-share ZIP file to your Desktop:\nCopy-Item -Path \"C:\\Users\\KRUTIKA SHIVANAND\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\queue-oracle.zip\" -Destination \"$HOME\\Desktop\\queue-oracle.zip\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### What Is Inside the Download:\n- `app.py` — Flask backend application & REST API server\n- `hospital.db` — SQLite database with seeded operational records\n- `models/wait_time_rf.joblib` — Trained Random Forest AI model artifact\n- `models/model_metrics.json` — Calculated validation metrics ($R^2 \\approx 0.996$, $\\text{MAE} \\approx 10\\text{ mins}$)\n- `dataset/synthetic_patients.csv` — 1,500 historical patient training records\n- `templates/index.html` — Full dashboard with all 14 working navigation sections\n- `static/css/` & `static/js/` — Styling and dynamic simulation & Chart.js scripts\n- `README.md` — Complete hackathon presentation guide & evaluation cheat-sheet","thinking":"The project files are now available on the user's computer. The files, both zipped and unzipped, are located in the specified directory. The user can access them through Windows File Explorer.\n\n\n"}
